+**A** describes the core-level stock calculation: carbon concentration is the fraction of dry soil mass that is carbon; bulk density converts sampled soil volume to dry soil mass; and depth determines the soil volume being considered. Consistent units and soil-layer treatment are essential. A local stock estimate can be scaled up only through a defensible spatial design or prediction model.
